picture-codex.md:102:I would **defer GPU rank infrastructure**. The completed logs show thousands of seconds in standard-basis construction before matrix rank is available. GPU acceleration cannot remove that polynomial bottleneck. First export a matrix whose exact rank dominates end-to-end cost; then compare a finite-field implementation against FLINT/LinBox, including transfer and certification. Floating-point rank and characteristic-two substitution would change the evidential problem. [`E8 timing:1–4`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/runs/e8_a2/out.log:1), [`W8 timing:1–4`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/runs/w8_a2/out.log:1), [`consult:440,470`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/codex-consult-v2.md:440)
picture-codex.md:104:I would also avoid rebuilding the whole algebra stack, repeating the old unrestricted graph elimination, launching extra sign-equivalent jobs, or treating `DegreeLimit` as protection for Macaulay2 `reesIdeal`: the installed implementation explicitly says that option has no effect. [`ReesAlgebra.m2:113–122`](/usr/share/Macaulay2/ReesAlgebra.m2:113)
picture-codex.md:106:Placement should follow the measured mechanism and an aggregate memory budget. The host incident involved several concurrent workloads, a terminal scope using about 64 GB plus 27 GB of swap, and an uncapped Singular job. The later W8 failure occurred inside its own 6-GiB cgroup, a different boundary. The record supports controlling concurrency; it does not identify one process as the sole cause of the terminal-scope kill. [`decision-record.md:125–136`](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:125)
picture-codex.md:112:| **Host** | Driver development; symmetry and relation checks; small target-ideal decomposition; VB completion experiments; short X/Iso structural probes | One heavy job at **8–16 GiB**, optionally one **4-GiB** small job. Keep the aggregate admitted algebra budget at **24 GiB** initially. Give exploratory certificates **15–60 minutes**; give VB A/B attempts **1–3 hours** before reviewing the result. |
picture-codex.md:114:| **Azure VM, one per region** | Large full-fiber saturation, E8-bar→N−, and matrix constructions that exceed Kaggle’s measured envelope | One heavy job per VM. Start at **64 GiB**, increasing toward **72 GiB** only after measuring operating-system headroom. Use **6–10-hour attempts**, stage exports, and an independent VM deallocation deadline. Run the E8-bar and W8 completion jobs sequentially. |
picture-codex.md:115:| **GitHub Actions** | Deterministic relation verification, provenance/schema checks, symmetry checks, small replay controls; scheduled bounded independent checks | **8–12 GiB** job budget. Keep ordinary PR additions short; use scheduled/manual jobs of **30 minutes–2 hours** for larger verification. The cited runner envelope is 16 GiB and six hours, leaving little room for discovery computations near that ceiling. |
picture-codex.md:121:The next concrete milestone should be **one complete, independently checked fiber receipt**, preferably E8-bar→VB if its small target presentation yields to structural recognition. That receipt should connect full algebra, embedded components, characteristic-zero verification, and the remaining real attachment obligation. It would validate the machinery needed to turn the other five rows from quadratic candidates into roadmap-item-6 evidence.
review-codex.md:3:1. **SERIOUS — degree-three agreement does not certify the whole fiber.** The W8 result says \(V(K_2)\) remains an upper bound “until degree 3 or method B closes it” ([decision-record.md:97](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:97)). Agreement at degree three establishes only \(K_3=(K_2)_3\); a new relation can first appear at a higher degree. The record correctly rejects the proposed regularity shortcut elsewhere ([decision-record.md:24](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:24)). Apply the existing finite-segment qualification consistently: X and Iso have no additional cubic relations, while their full fiber ideals remain unresolved ([decision-record.md:79](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:79), [decision-record.md:83](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:83)).
