review-codex.md:14:   - For **reduced support equality**, X has an irreducible arithmetic quadratic support of projective dimension three and degree twelve ([pC_xm_reduce.log:1](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/probes/pC_xm_reduce.log:1)). A certified three-dimensional family of actual limits dense in that support would establish support equality. That certificate would leave scheme structure and the full Hilbert series unresolved ([codex-consult-v2.md:141](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/codex-consult-v2.md:141)).
