review-codex.md:29:**Method A passes the code-level checks.** The quadratic template constructs \(J+\mathfrak mP_d\) and reduces products modulo \(J\) ([a2_body.sing:3](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/templates/a2_body.sing:3)). The cubic code uses actual `kbase` monomials, so `leadexp` retains their entire exponent information; multiplication follows those exponents and reduces after every factor ([s1/input.sing:12](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/runs/s1/input.sing:12)). Certified previous relations give local generation by Nakayama. The resulting product quotient is annihilated by \(\mathfrak m\), making global membership sufficient.
review-codex.md:31:The retained normal-form files use the signed integer coefficients, explicit multiplication, and powers that the parsers handle ([rank_nf.py:13](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/probes/rank_nf.py:13), [relations_nf.py:16](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/probes/relations_nf.py:16)). Independent coefficient-matrix checks confirmed complete relation spaces of dimensions **69, 148, and 144** for X, E8, and W8. The transpose and nullspace-column orientation correctly compute the left kernel ([relations_nf.py:40](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/probes/relations_nf.py:40)).
review-codex.md:33:**Method B also passes.** The colon test establishes \((J:g)=J\), a sufficient global nonzerodivisor condition. The template then forms \(H\), saturates by \(g\), and specializes every source variable to zero ([b_body.sing:5](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/templates/b_body.sing:5), [b_body.sing:11](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/templates/b_body.sing:11)). Rees formation commutes with localization at the origin. After specialization, every inverted source polynomial with nonzero constant term becomes an invertible scalar. Components confined away from the origin therefore contribute nothing to this fiber. The installed `sat` returns an ideal, matching the assignment ([elim.lib:717](/usr/share/singular/LIB/elim.lib:717)).
review-codex.md:39:- E8’s tested substitution matches \(J\) up to sign and fails all 21 generator sign comparisons ([e8.sing:6](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/runs/s0b/e8.sing:6)). Finding 2 states the resulting evidential boundary.
review-codex.md:41:Several smaller claims need narrower wording. Iso’s **23 is the quadratic scheme’s degree**, rather than a relation degree ([purpose.md:17](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/purpose.md:17), [pD_iso.log:1](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/probes/pD_iso.log:1)). The reported “std seconds” are cumulative elapsed times because the timer starts before product construction ([a2_body.sing:2](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/templates/a2_body.sing:2)). The X timeout has exit 124 recorded, while its cited log records pivot selection rather than the claimed 6.9G peak ([try3h/rc:1](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/runs/s2/try3h/rc:1), [try3h/out.log:21](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/runs/s2/try3h/out.log:21)). Finally, GTZ coordinate-change densification remains an inferred cause, although the summary presents it as established ([first-principles-plan.md:22](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/first-principles-plan.md:22), [decision-record.md:111](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:111)).
review-codex.md:43:My ranking for the remaining work is an expected-value judgment; comparative completion costs remain unmeasured:
review-codex.md:45:1. **Test localized E8 generator equivalence and pursue an X completion certificate.** The former may eliminate duplicate work; the latter builds on the inexpensive known X support. Investigate the colon/symmetric-algebra or dense-family certificates before another unchanged saturation extension.
review-codex.md:46:2. **Give Iso method B a bounded completion attempt.** Its cubic piece is already certified; repeating the stopped local-syzygy calculation adds little ([decision-record.md:83](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:83)).
review-codex.md:47:3. **Compute E8-bar N− degree two if the equivalence test leaves the row independent.** Use that result to validate method B before assigning more full-saturation time ([decision-record.md:145](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/decision-record.md:145)).
review-codex.md:48:4. **Extend E8-bar degree three before W8 degree three when a further finite piece answers a concrete question.** Their candidate counts are 225 and 600, but observed product-building times caution against predicting runtime from counts alone ([e8_a3/out.log:1](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/runs/e8_a3/out.log:1), [w8_a3/out.log:1](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/runs/w8_a3/out.log:1)).
review-codex.md:49:5. **Keep VM 2’s E8-then-W8 saturation experiments bounded and sequential.** Their value is full completion, with the completed method-A pieces serving as cross-checks ([vm2-fiber-b.md:22](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/azure-cases/vm2-fiber-b.md:22)).
